## 1. NON-NEGOTIABLE TECHNOLOGY CONSTRAINTS

### Required architecture
- Frontend: React + TypeScript.
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript.
- Database access: Prisma ORM with versioned migrations.
- Database: PostgreSQL hosted on a self-managed VPS.
- Document storage: private server-side filesystem, with paths and metadata stored in PostgreSQL.
- Deployment: Docker Compose or an equally reproducible deployment approach appropriate to the chosen VPS.
- HTTPS in production.
- Local libraries for PDF processing, Excel processing and OCR where feasible.

### Absolutely prohibited
- Firebase Authentication.
- Cloud Firestore.
- Firebase Realtime Database.
- Firebase Storage.
- Firebase Cloud Functions.
- Firebase Admin SDK or other Firebase SDKs.
- Firebase configuration files, rules, deployment configuration or environment variables.
- Supabase or another third-party hosted database service.
- Gemini API, OpenAI API or other external/paid AI APIs.
- Cloud OCR, external document-extraction APIs, or external bank/document integrations.
- Any hidden external service required for the core business workflow.

The application may use its own internal backend endpoints to communicate between its frontend, backend and PostgreSQL. These are part of the custom application and are not external third-party APIs.

Do not store the production business database solely in localStorage or IndexedDB. Browser storage may be used for temporary UI state only, not as the authoritative record.

Do not put database credentials, session secrets or other server secrets in frontend code.

If a requested capability cannot be implemented under these constraints, explain the limitation and provide a working local/server-side alternative or a clearly marked manual-review workflow. Never silently add a prohibited service.

