## 7. DOCUMENT MANAGEMENT

Required document categories:
- Commercial Invoice.
- Shipping Bill.
- FIRC/payment evidence.
- Bill of Lading/transport document.
- BRC Copy 1.
- BRC Copy 2.
- Additional documents.

Commercial Invoice, Shipping Bill and FIRC/payment evidence are required in the standard shipment workflow. Bill of Lading and BRC requirements must follow their defined optional/conditional rules.

### Mandatory FIRC rule
A valid FIRC/payment record must be linked before a shipment can be saved.

The system must distinguish the existence of FIRC evidence from the amount allocated to an invoice. A payment may be shared across multiple invoices using separate allocation records.

### BRC rules
- Single mode: exactly one BRC file.
- Multiple mode: exactly two separate BRC files.
- Keep the two files separate, independently named and downloadable.
- Do not silently combine two files into one.
- Do not infer a payment amount from BRC files.
- Preserve BRC number, document/issue date and realisation date as separate fields.
- Do not assume the meaning of each file in Multiple mode until confirmed by the business.

### File storage
Store files on the server in a private directory organised by financial year and normalised invoice/shipment identity, for example:

`storage/FY2026-27/SKE-26-27-020/Commercial-Invoice.pdf`

Use database metadata for all document associations. Metadata must include document type, original filename, safe stored filename/path, shipment/payment association, uploaded by, uploaded at, version, size and relevant status.

Provide individual upload, preview, download, replacement and authorised removal actions. Preserve audit history for replacement/removal; do not destroy the only audit evidence of a prior version.

Do not expose files using public or guessable URLs. Every file access must validate the signed-in user's permission and the document's database relationship.

Validate file types and sizes. Prevent path traversal and unsafe file handling.

