## 8. DOCUMENT EXTRACTION WITHOUT EXTERNAL APIs

Use local/server-side libraries only.

### Extraction strategy
- Commercial Invoice: local PDF text extraction and rules for known layouts.
- Shipping Bill: local PDF text extraction and rules for supported layouts.
- FIRC: rules for the known bank template.
- BRC/eBRC: extract references, dates and amounts from supported text layouts.
- Bill of Lading: local text extraction; scanned files may require OCR or manual review.
- Scanned PDFs: use a locally installed OCR engine only if it is actually integrated and tested.

Every extracted field must be editable. Display extracted values and the source document side by side where practical.

Use review states such as:
- Extracted.
- Needs review.
- Missing.
- Confirmed.
- Manually entered.

Where feasible, retain source page and text snippets to support review. If confidence scoring is unavailable, use a review status rather than inventing a confidence percentage.

Never guess unreadable fields. Keep them blank and highlight them. Require an Admin to confirm extracted fields before saving the shipment.

Provide manual entry and correction as a complete fallback. The application must remain usable when extraction fails.

Do not use an external AI API as a fallback.

