## 10. FINANCIAL CALCULATIONS AND VALIDATION

Implement authoritative calculations in the backend.

### Required calculations
- Invoice balance due based on the approved invoice-currency allocation method.
- Available payment balance.
- Payment received totals.
- Part-paid/full-paid/excess status.
- Received exchange rate where valid USD and INR values exist.
- FOB INR comparison against source USD and Shipping Bill rate.
- Incentive outstanding balances.
- Applicable tracker formula equivalents.
- Summary totals and reports.

### Required checks
- Invoice identity in the document versus the selected shipment.
- Invoice item total versus invoice total, when line-item data is present.
- Verified payment against invoice value.
- Shipping Bill USD/rate/FOB INR comparison.
- Invoice date versus Shipping Bill date.
- Financial-year consistency.
- Consignee and bank master matches.
- IRM date-prefix check against FIRC credit date where the source convention supports it.
- BRC missing references/dates and upcoming deadlines.
- Cross-document discrepancies, including vessel discrepancies where present.
- Duplicate invoice identities within a financial year.

Distinguish:
1. Blocking errors that prevent saving.
2. Warnings that require review but do not automatically prevent saving.
3. Informational comparisons.

Do not silently change a source value to make a validation pass. Preserve source-specific values and display the discrepancy.

Do not label an arithmetic difference as a confirmed forex gain without an approved methodology.

