## 17. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is not complete until the applicable tests pass.

### Architecture
- No Firebase or Supabase dependencies or configuration.
- No external/paid API required for the core workflow.
- Frontend and backend start successfully.
- PostgreSQL migrations run successfully.
- Records persist across browser sessions and server restarts.
- Private files persist and remain associated with the correct database records.

### Permissions
- Super Admin can manage Admin accounts.
- Admin cannot manage Admin/Super Admin accounts.
- Viewer cannot mutate records through UI or direct requests.
- Every document download checks permissions.

### Shipments and documents
- Shipment save is blocked without linked valid FIRC/payment evidence.
- Single BRC mode rejects zero or more than one file.
- Multiple BRC mode rejects any count other than two.
- Uploaded files are linked to the correct shipment/payment.
- Replacing a file preserves the required audit/version history.
- Missing or unreadable extracted fields are never guessed.

### Payments
- One payment can be allocated across multiple invoices.
- Available balance and invoice balance are correct.
- Over-allocation is rejected.
- Concurrent allocation attempts cannot overspend a payment.
- Reversals/edits update balances and audit history.
- Payment value, credit, issue and realisation dates remain distinct.

### Data and exports
- Invoice-number normalisation passes positive and negative test cases.
- Duplicate invoice detection respects financial-year boundaries.
- Source-specific exchange rates are preserved.
- Historical rows without FIRC are excluded.
- Exported values match approved source mappings and calculations.
- Test results identify unsupported workbook/macros behaviour.

### Operations
- Build and automated tests run successfully.
- Backup and restore procedures are tested.
- Deployment steps are documented.
- No production credentials are committed.
- All incomplete features are explicitly listed.

